# "When Enduring Innocence dies, if it was a creature, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control. It's an enchantment." The
# intervening "if" (CR 603.4) is judged on what it was on the battlefield: Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills the creature on turn 2 and it comes
# back an enchantment; on turn 4 Bot2 Disenchants it and, no longer a creature when it goes to the graveyard, it stays there.

